<title>ITALY: Minimum rate 6.75 pct at Italy BOT buyback.</title>
<headline>Minimum rate 6.75 pct at Italy BOT buyback.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The minimum rate at today's 2.0 trillion lire buyback of short term Treasury bills (BOTs) by the Bank of Italy was 6.75 percent compared with 6.80 percent previously, the Bank said.</p>
<p>The average rate was 6.78 percent also against 6.86 percent at the previous operation for 1.50 trillion lire on January 29.</p>
<p>The Bank said it received 16 bids of which eight were met in full and five in part.</p>
</text>
